{
  "title": "109: al-Kaaferoon الكافرون",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْكٰفِرُوْنَۙ‏(1)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL KAAFEROONA. \nSay: O unbelievers! \nلَاۤ اَعْبُدُ مَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(2)\nLAA A-A’BODO MAA TA’BODOONA. \nI do not serve that which you serve, \nوَلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عٰبِدُوْنَ مَاۤ اَعْبُدُ ۚ‏(3)\nWA LAA ANTUM A’ABEDOONA MAA A-A’BOD. \nNor do you serve Him Whom I serve: \nوَلَاۤ اَنَا عَابِدٌ مَّا عَبَدْتُّمْۙ‏(4)\nWA LAA ANAA A’ABEDUM MAA A’BAT-TUM. \nNor am I going to serve that which you serve, \nوَ لَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عٰبِدُوْنَ مَاۤ اَعْبُدُ ؕ‏(5)\nWA LAA ANTUM A’ABEDOONA MAA A-A’BOD. \nNor are you going to serve Him Whom I serve: \nلَكُمْ دِيْنُكُمْ وَلِىَ دِيْنِ‏(6)\nLAKUM DEENOKUM WA LEYA DEEN.\nYou shall have your religion and I shall have my religion.",
  "merits": "This Surah is ‘Makki’ and has 6 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that reciting this Surah carries the reward of reciting a quarter of the Holy Qur’an. The recitation of this Surah drives away Shaitan and keeps one safe from Shirk.\nIt is also among the five Surahs that have been recommended to be recited during a journey, the others being [Surah al-Nasr](A114), al-Tawheed, al-Falaq and al-Naas. Reciting Surah al-Kaaferoon and al-Tawheed in compulsory prayers is a means for forgiveness of sins for the reciter, his parents and his children. If a person dies after reciting this Surah, it is as if he has died a martyr. Recitation of this Surah before sleeping keeps one safe the whole night."
